# affected, medium(Red Hat): libc-bin, libc6 - glibc: glibc: Heap Buffer Overflow in `scanf` with `%mc` format specifier and...
# function of scanf family is imported by e.g. nginx-module-otel
CVE-2026-5450 exp:2026-09-22

# affected, medium(Red Hat): libc-bin, libc6 - glibc: glibc: Information disclosure or denial of service via ungetwc function with...
# function ungetwc is loaded dynamically by libstdc++ which is loaded by nginx-module-otel
CVE-2026-5928 exp:2026-09-22

# affected, high: bsdutils, libblkid1, libmount1, libsmartcols1, login, mount - util-linux
# No fix published by Debian yet (status "affected", no fixed version). The PEP runs
# unprivileged and invokes neither the mount/nsenter helpers nor login.
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-09-22

# affected, high: libsystemd0 - systemd: systemd-homed local privilege escalation
# No fix published by Debian yet. systemd-homed is not present in the image.
CVE-2026-16742 exp:2026-09-22

# fixed, high: libpcre2-8-0, libpcre2-32-0 - pcre2: out-of-bounds write via crafted regular
# expressions (86145) and memory corruption in pcre2_jit_match (89161). Fix is available in
# Debian trixie (10.46-1~deb13u2) and lands with the next base-image rebuild on main;
# these entries only bridge until that image lands.
CVE-2026-86145 exp:2026-09-22
CVE-2026-89161 exp:2026-09-22
